<title>TAIWAN: Taiwan says to cut reserve requirements in H2.</title>
<headline>Taiwan says to cut reserve requirements in H2.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1997-07-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan central bank vice governor Hsu Chia-tung on Friday said the central bank would keep its promise to cut banks' reserve requirements in the second half of 1997.</p>
<p>&quot;The central bank will definitely choose an appropriate time to cut banks' reserve requirements in the second half of this year,&quot; Hsu told a news conference.</p>
<p>When asked whether the central bank planned to cut the key rates more than once, Hsu said: &quot;We will discuss this later.&quot;</p>
<p>The central bank has repeatedly said lowering banks' reserve requirements was its policy. -- Taipei Newsroom (5080815)</p>
